  "body": "![Comparison](https://imgur.com/FTD8uKA.png)\n\n[modrinth](https://modrinth.com/resourcepack/low-fire-pack) [curseforge](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/texture-packs/low-fire)\n\n> #### Low Fire reduces the height of the fire in first-person, making sure it doesn't distract your view during gameplay while keeping the original block fire texture on the floor.\n\n- **Fire is 6 pixels lower than vanilla! That's 37.5% lower!**\n- **Fire is only lower in first-person and keeps the default block texture.**\n\n<br>\n\n### How it works 🧠\n-   The model file separates the entity fire and block fire, so you can change the entity fire without messing with the block fire.\n\n##### This resource pack is always up to date and regularly tested to check for version compatibility, new file updates, and bugs.\n\n### License **(ARR)** 📜\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>License</summary>\n\n- Feel free to use, modify, or share this project in any of your modpacks or resource packs as long as proper credit is given to me.\n- You may not sell or use this resource pack in any way that requires payment to access it.\n\n##### For any other concerns, feel free to message me on discord **(@Oculie)**.\n</details>",
